WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:04.820
Last year, I called the Pixel 3 XL the worst
flagship phone I’ve ever used.

00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:09.720
I admit I was very harsh in my review, which
got a lot of hateful comments, but I had to

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:13.980
stand by my opinions not only because the
3 XL had a lot of software issues, but because

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:18.699
it was also quite a bit behind hardware-wise
when you consider the $900 price point.

00:00:18.699 --> 00:00:23.460
So what about half a year later, now that
Google released the 3a and 3aXL?

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:28.249
Well, to be honest, my mind is completely
changed this time around, and this time I’m

00:00:28.249 --> 00:00:30.359
calling the 3a XL Budget Perfection.

00:00:30.359 --> 00:00:36.270
The 3a doesn’t have top of the line specs
like the 3, the CPU is a bit weaker, the graphics

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:41.400
are even behind the Pixel 2, The display is
of lower quality and as are the speakers.

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:46.390
There's no wireless charging, no IP water
resistance rating, and the phone is made of

00:00:46.390 --> 00:00:47.390
plastic.

00:00:47.390 --> 00:00:50.910
But at half the price, all those sins are
forgiven and if you compare the features to

00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:54.550
other similarly priced phones, the 3a really
shines.

00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:57.820
Now there are a few things I wish Google did
differently, and there are some people who

00:00:57.820 --> 00:01:01.790
I wouldn’t recommend it to, which I’ll
cover in just a bit, but overall, this phone

00:01:01.790 --> 00:01:03.770
is a winner and I would highly recommend it.

00:01:03.770 --> 00:01:07.909
I don’t want to get too much into specs,
but we have the same rear camera, with a single

00:01:07.909 --> 00:01:13.609
front that's wider than the pixels 3’s standard
which was a smart move, rear fingerprint scanner,

00:01:13.609 --> 00:01:16.590
Google assistant squeeze feature, and the
same 4GB of RAM.

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:21.719
What really matters is the real world experience,
how is it to use the phone day to day, and

00:01:21.719 --> 00:01:24.229
I have to say that is really good.

00:01:24.229 --> 00:01:29.490
No not as good as a proper flagship like the
S10+ or 7 Pro, but still good and for the

00:01:29.490 --> 00:01:31.090
price tag, excellent.

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:35.829
RAM management wasn’t an issue for me, and
the UI was smoother than the Pixel 3’s.

00:01:35.829 --> 00:01:41.569
The CPU is slower so its not that, but thanks
to Google Optimizing and fixing software bugs

00:01:41.569 --> 00:01:43.009
ever since their flagships launched.

00:01:43.009 --> 00:01:47.469
Google made a smart choice to put spend money
where it matters and is most noticeable.

00:01:47.469 --> 00:01:50.229
The Camera, Display, and speakers.

00:01:50.229 --> 00:01:52.969
The things you actually interact with most.

00:01:52.969 --> 00:01:57.670
As I mentioned the display and speakers aren’t
as good as the 3’s, but the OLED screen

00:01:57.670 --> 00:02:01.850
and stereo speakers definitely are close and
fight above their price point.

00:02:01.850 --> 00:02:05.259
The photo quality is really good, basically
the same as the Pixel 3’s.

00:02:05.259 --> 00:02:08.930
The algorithms have been tweaked over time
and I noticed images don’t have the same

00:02:08.930 --> 00:02:12.410
strong bias towards cool white balances which
Im glad they tweaked.

00:02:12.410 --> 00:02:17.080
Since we have a single lens camera, zoom shots
are still behind phones with a dedicated telephoto

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:21.110
lens, but because of Google photo stacking
they look better than then other single systems

00:02:21.110 --> 00:02:22.350
like the XR.

00:02:22.350 --> 00:02:28.560
Portrait photos oldy now use a 2x digital
crop instead of the 1.25x the Pixel 3 used.

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:32.940
I really liked the slight crop of the 3, it
limited distortion for close ups but still

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:34.870
gave a high quality great looking wide portrait.

00:02:34.870 --> 00:02:35.870
Usind a 2x crops gives a similar field of
view to the iPhone XS which is close to a

00:02:35.870 --> 00:02:36.870
real 50mm lens but cropping so much on a wide
lens reduces the image quality and make noise

00:02:36.870 --> 00:02:37.870
more visible.

00:02:37.870 --> 00:02:38.870
Don’t get me wrong, the photos don’t look
bad, and in low light will still look better

00:02:38.870 --> 00:02:39.870
than the XS’s due to a faster lens, I just
wish they gave us an option to choose the

00:02:39.870 --> 00:02:40.870
crop.

00:02:40.870 --> 00:02:41.870
Video recording is still a few years behind
the flagships, with no 4K 60 and poor mic

00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:42.870
quality but thats passible at this price point,
just like not having a telephoto or wide angle

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:43.870
lens, and other things like 4GB of RAM, and
a thicker bezel.

00:02:43.870 --> 00:02:48.380
This phone will take better photos than any
phone under $500, and many that are far more

00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:49.380
expensive.

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:51.170
My only other complaint is the shutter lag.

00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:54.200
It seems worst than the Pixel 3, and far behind
the flagships.

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:58.130
In this side by side I pressed the shutter
right when elon was at the top of the swing,

00:02:58.130 --> 00:03:03.140
The iPhone grabbed the image instantly ever
time since its actually constantly taking

00:03:03.140 --> 00:03:05.210
phtos and just saves the photo when you press.

00:03:05.210 --> 00:03:09.420
The Samsung and Oneplus are behind but no
where near as much as the 3a XL which took

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:11.690
the image almost a second later.

00:03:11.690 --> 00:03:15.290
I complained about this in my S10+ review,
since I noticed myself missing shots of my

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:18.540
kids in action which I would have properly
captured on the iPhone.

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:22.910
If you have little kids, pets, or shoot other
quick moving subject this could be a deal

00:03:22.910 --> 00:03:23.910
breaker.

00:03:23.910 --> 00:03:27.750
Check out or detailed photo comparison to
see how it stacks up to 3 very impressive

00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:29.500
flagships after this video.

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:31.410
Let just back to the design of the phone.

00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:35.010
Google needed to cut costs so the phone is
made of plastic.

00:03:35.010 --> 00:03:38.450
Some reviewers said it feels just as good
as the 3, I can see where they are coming

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:43.540
from because of the frosted back but I can
definitely tell its not as premium.

00:03:43.540 --> 00:03:47.730
With that said, it doesn’t feel cheap at
all, and most people will put a case on it

00:03:47.730 --> 00:03:52.450
and then there's not difference.

00:03:52.450 --> 00:03:54.800
On the plus side, the headphone jack is back.

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:59.180
It makes a ton of sense why, if you’re buying
a budget phone the chances of you not owning

00:03:59.180 --> 00:04:00.850
Bluetooth headphones is much higher.

00:04:00.850 --> 00:04:04.290
The forehead and chin are quite large, but
so where the pixel 3’s after people used

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:08.870
software to cover up that huge notch so the
end results were the same.

00:04:08.870 --> 00:04:11.510
At this price point, it makes more sense.

00:04:11.510 --> 00:04:15.400
On the positive side, the batteries are large
and that's a huge plus.

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:22.240
The 3a XL’s is 3700MAh and paired with a
less powerful thus less power draining processor

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:25.630
and lower rez display means it last a long
time.

00:04:25.630 --> 00:04:29.500
If you're a power user on a budget it will
last you a full day.

00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:34.900
MrWhostheBoss did a battery shootout and the
3a XL lasted for 8 hours of heavy screen on

00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:39.780
time, longer than any phone hes ever tested
and even beating out the ZenPhone 6 that has

00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:41.660
a 5000Mah Battery!

00:04:41.660 --> 00:04:46.490
For regular users, the 3a which has a smaller
battery but a more manageable size should

00:04:46.490 --> 00:04:47.490
last all day as well.

00:04:47.490 --> 00:04:48.490
If your a gamer the weaker graphics end up
extending battery life while gaming by quite

00:04:48.490 --> 00:04:49.490
a bit, but the graphics quality is noticeably
lower as well.

00:04:49.490 --> 00:04:50.970
If you’ll be playing a lot of games I’d
suggest picking something else up, maybe the

00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:53.040
RazerPhone which is now priced similarly.

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:57.310
If you want to know more check out our gaming
comparison to the Pixel 3 after this video.

00:04:57.310 --> 00:05:00.842
So all of that said, I think Google made a
genius move bringing out the Pixel 3a XL,

00:05:00.842 --> 00:05:01.940
and I hope they continue to focus on this
mid-range price point.

00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:05.370
When you consider the price point and feature
set, a lot of smart decisions were made on

00:05:05.370 --> 00:05:07.340
where to focus and where to cut cost.

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:11.250
For most people, the 3a and 3aXL will get
the job done, and I would recommend it to

00:05:11.250 --> 00:05:14.910
almost everyone who’s looking to buy at
this price point other than those who need

00:05:14.910 --> 00:05:18.500
something with minimal camera shutter lag
or hardcore phone gamers.

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:22.190
Google has a real winner in their hands, and
now that its at every Major carrier in the

00:05:22.190 --> 00:05:24.380
states its going to be in a lot of others.

00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:28.130
Thanks for checking out our review, if you
want to pick up a Pixel 3 a or 3a XL we have

00:05:28.130 --> 00:05:31.250
a link to some great deals down in the description
below.

00:05:31.250 --> 00:05:34.980
Click right over here to subscribe and if
you want to see out detailed camera comparison

00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:38.840
click right over there, this has been Max
with Max Tech and I’ll see you in the next

00:05:38.840 --> 00:05:42.320
video!

